==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wargod Yukimura''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Immortal Yukimura''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Sanada Yukimura's points of interest include his high speed, fast foreswing, high damage and sheer disposability for an uber. He's best suited to either deal heavy damage to the enemy base or to slow down slow-attacking, slow-moving or long-ranged enemy units such as [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]], making him also good for cheesing strategies. This unit's usage is also similar to [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], so you can use him as a replacement if you do not have Awakened Bahamut yet, and can also use both together for extra destruction.

Sanada Yukimura's massive damage against Dark enemies can be helpful against the likes of [[Bun Bun Black]] and [[Shadow Boxer K]] by being a reliable knockback pusher, as his foreswing allows him to get an easy hit on, while his backswing prevents him from being hit by attacks after dealing damage as your other units catch up. Most Dark enemies have a high KB count, so he could reliably ward them off with his high damage.

==='''True Form'''===
Immortal Yukimura has 50% more attack power, which is a massive improvement for a True Form evolution. This, combined with the added movement speed, can greatly improve his performance on average and bring forth further annihilation. He can also serve as a substitute for Awakened Bahamut or even pair up with Bahamut as Yukimura has a bit more health, which means he can survive certain attacks like a 150% Director Kurosawah.

In comparison to a Lv. 30 Awakened Bahamut, a Lv. 40 Immortal Yukimura has less than half the DPS, one less knockback, and a lower range, but he makes up for it with his superior health and movement speed, not to mention his having of a lower cost and almost half the recharge time. Additionally, he wipes he floor against Bahamut when dealing with Dark enemies with his Massive Damage ability.

Additionally, Immortal Yukimura and Awakened Bahamut combine with [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] to form the [[Heavenly Kings (Combo)|Heavenly Kings]] [[Cat Combo|Combo]], which boosts the Massive Damage ability by 10%, being quite convenient for a Combo that uses some of the strongest rushers in the game.

==='''Talents'''===
Immortal Yukimura relies a lot on his stats, so you can't go wrong with Attack Up, HP  Buff or [[Strengthen]], as all these [[Talents]] greatly improve this unit's performance on the battlefield, especially as he also benefits from Catseyes.

Ignore the last two Talents (Resist Freeze, Resist Slow), as Yukimura doesn't live long, so he's unlikely to need them, if well timed. They can still come in handy in rare occasions, but only consider investing in them if your Yukimura is properly boosted.

